<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giuseppe Prina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1766">1766</a>–<a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giuseppe Prina was finance minister of the Napoleonic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> from 1805. His heavy taxes, raised to pay for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s wars, made him widely hated. After Napoleon's abdication, a crowd in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> lynched him on 20 April 1814, and the disorder helped Austrian troops take control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuseppe-prina.jpg" alt="Giuseppe Prina" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giuseppe_Prina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
